@startuml

title Keeping the installation's secrets: what the person does, and what each screen refuses

start
:opens Secrets;
if (holds vault::secrets:write?) then (yes)
    :sees Add beside the list;
else (no)
    :Add is not drawn at all;
endif
:scans the list: name, consumer, current version, key version;
:opens one secret, and reads its version stream;
if (asks to reveal the value?) then (yes)
    if (holds vault::secrets:read?) then (yes)
        :the value is masked until the ask;
        :the ask is recorded twice:
        the vault records the resolve,
        the gateway records the person;
    else (no)
        :the control is not drawn;
    endif
else (no)
    :the value stays masked;
endif
fork
    :replaces a value in a dialog, and Save waits on the rule;
fork again
    :registers a consumer with its public key, or disables one;
fork again
    :rotates the protecting key as one audited act;
end fork
:leaves the area;
stop

@enduml
